{"name":"Cape Lee","hex":"#50818b","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"cape","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A piece or point of land, extending beyond the adjacent coast into a sea or lake; a promontory; a headland."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A sleeveless garment or part of a garment, hanging from the neck over the back, arms, and shoulders.","A superhero."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cape"},{"term":"lee","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Lyélé."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A protected cove or harbor, out of the wind.","The side of the ship away from the wind."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lee"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cape","blocks":[{"text":"A cape is a clothing accessory or a sleeveless outer garment of any length that hangs loosely and connects either at the neck or shoulders. They usually cover the back, shoulders, and arms. They come in a variety of styles and have been used throughout history for many different reasons."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cape"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9f/Batman_and_Robin_1966.JPG/500px-Batman_and_Robin_1966.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9f/Batman_and_Robin_1966.JPG/500px-Batman_and_Robin_1966.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Batman and Robin","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABatman_and_Robin_1966.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a2/Dracula_Cape.jpg/120px-Dracula_Cape.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a2/Dracula_Cape.jpg/250px-Dracula_Cape.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wiki